Phase 3:

The main drawback of Merge Sort is that it requires extra memory for its temporary array. 
\Selection Sort works directly with the original array and does not need much additional space.
If a computer has very limited RAM, Merge Sort could use memory that is needed for other tasks. 
Even though Merge Sort is faster with larger arrays, Selection Sort may be a better choice when memory is more important.

Selection Sort became much slower as the array size increased, which is what I expected from O(N²).
